Interior illustration of a small artisan workshop that has been violently ransacked. Perspective view from the doorway looking in.

SCENE: A picture framer's workshop, daytime. The door is wide open. Morning light streams in from a high window on the left, illuminating the destruction.

DESTRUCTION: Wooden picture frames broken and scattered on the floor. A workbench overturned on its side, tools (hammers, small saws, clamps) spilled everywhere. Drawers pulled out and emptied — papers and wood shavings on the floor. A shelf on the back wall with frames still hanging at odd angles, some fallen. A pot of wood glue spilled, dripping off the bench. Sawdust and splinters everywhere.

DETAILS: The frames on the walls are the only things still somewhat intact — ornate, gilded (chipping), various sizes. One large frame on the back wall is cracked in half, as if someone checked behind it. A small stool knocked over. Drag marks on the dusty floor leading toward the back door (barely visible).

ATMOSPHERE: Violence happened here, but it's over. The room is still and silent. Dust motes in the light. The smell of wood glue and broken varnish. No blood — this was a kidnapping, not a murder.

STYLE: Realistic fantasy illustration, painterly. Warm morning light contrasting with the cold violence of the scene. Color palette: warm wood tones, golden light, dark shadows in corners.

MOOD: Unsettling calm after chaos. Something bad happened here and the victim is gone.
